Review written to `docs/reviews/hpxml/hpxml-04-foundation-wall-area-zero.md`.

**Summary**: 1 high-severity finding. The `parse_boundary_area` function at `building.rs:1307` silently defaults FoundationWall and Slab areas to `0.0` when the `<Area>` element is missing — no warning, no error. All other boundary types (walls, roofs, floors, etc.) produce a hard `HpxmlError::Parse` for the same defect. OCHRE accesses the area via direct dict key access (`hpxml.py:140`), which raises a `KeyError` — also a hard failure. Recommendations: add at minimum a `tracing::warn!` diagnostic when falling back to 0.0, and consider aligning with other boundary types for a hard parse error.
